# LF in the working tree on every platform. Git for Windows installs with
# core.autocrlf=true, which would check text out as CRLF: every shell script
# then fails on `set -u\r`, and files the app embeds with include_str! (the
# default Dockerfile, hook scripts) change bytes, and with them the Docker
# image tag hash. See docs/ideas/windows.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts keep CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.caf binary
*.woff2 binary
*.iip binary
